From: RelicOS <relicos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: odroid_go2: add R36S board-detect entry

The R36S is an RK3326 handheld that reuses the ODROID-GO Advance
board-detection scheme: a resistor on SARADC channel 0 identifies the
board. The reference unit reads 166 (measured over serial on 2026-08-29
under a known-good vendor boot chain, and again under this U-Boot, which
stopped at "Unable to detect device type: -19"). Arch-R maps the window
140-190 (nominal 165) to the R36S, which agrees with the measurement.

Add a table entry so rk_board_late_init() succeeds. The fdtfile keeps
pointing at the odroid-go2 devicetree: mainline carries no R36S dts and
this port does not consume fdtfile yet.

With the +-50 tolerance the R36S window (117-215) overlaps the GO Super
window (36-134) over 117-134; real readings (85 and 166) sit more than
30 counts away from the ambiguous band, so the overlap is accepted
rather than worked around.
---
diff --git a/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c b/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
index ae32ea8..4351de2 100644
--- a/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
+++ b/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ enum oga_device_id {
 	OGA = 1,
 	OGA_V11,
 	OGS,
+	R36S,
 };
 
 /*
@@ -52,6 +53,12 @@ static const struct oga_model oga_model_details[] = {
 		"ODROID-GO Super",
 		DTB_DIR "rk3326-odroid-go3.dtb",
 	},
+	[R36S] = {
+		166,
+		"rk3326-r36s",
+		"R36S",
+		DTB_DIR "rk3326-odroid-go2.dtb",
+	},
 };
 
 static int oga_read_board_id(void)
